<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>RAG Simulator | Interactive Learning Lab</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

  <style>
    * {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    :root {
      --bg: #07111f;
      --panel: rgba(17, 25, 40, 0.78);
      --border: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      --text: #f5f7ff;
      --muted: #9fb0d3;
      --primary: #4ade80;
      --secondary: #60a5fa;
      --purple: #8b5cf6;
      --danger: #fb7185;
      --glass: blur(16px);
      --shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
    }

    body {
      font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(96,165,250,0.2), transparent 20%),
        radial-gradient(circle at bottom right, rgba(139,92,246,0.2), transparent 25%),
        var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      min-height: 100vh;
      overflow-x: hidden;
    }

    .container {
      width: 95%;
      max-width: 1500px;
      margin: 30px auto;
    }

    .hero {
      padding: 40px;
      border-radius: 28px;
      background: var(--panel);
      backdrop-filter: var(--glass);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .hero::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      width: 500px;
      height: 500px;
      background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(74,222,128,0.1), transparent 70%);
      top: -250px;
      right: -200px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 64px;
      font-weight: 800;
      line-height: 1;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      letter-spacing: -2px;
    }

    .gradient {
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--primary), var(--secondary), var(--purple));
      -webkit-background-clip: text;
      -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    }

    .subtitle {
      max-width: 1000px;
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 18px;
    }

    .layout {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 380px 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .sidebar,
    .main {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .card {
      background: var(--panel);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      backdrop-filter: var(--glass);
      border-radius: 24px;
      padding: 24px;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .card-title {
      font-size: 22px;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .dot {
      width: 12px;
      height: 12px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
      box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(74,222,128,0.8);
    }

    textarea {
      width: 100%;
      min-height: 170px;
      resize: vertical;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
      border-radius: 18px;
      padding: 18px;
      color: white;
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      outline: none;
      transition: 0.3s ease;
    }

    textarea:focus,
    input:focus {
      border-color: rgba(96,165,250,0.5);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(96,165,250,0.12);
    }

    input {
      width: 100%;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 16px;
      color: white;
      font-size: 15px;
      outline: none;
      transition: 0.3s ease;
    }

    .button-row {
      display: flex;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 16px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    button {
      border: none;
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 14px 18px;
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 700;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: 0.3s ease;
    }

    .primary-btn {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
      color: #07111f;
    }

    .secondary-btn {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
      color: white;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
    }

    button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }

    .pipeline {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
      gap: 16px;
    }

    .step {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
      border-radius: 22px;
      padding: 20px;
      position: relative;
      min-height: 150px;
      transition: 0.35s ease;
    }

    .step.active {
      border-color: rgba(74,222,128,0.5);
      transform: translateY(-4px);
      box-shadow: 0 0 25px rgba(74,222,128,0.18);
    }

    .step-number {
      width: 38px;
      height: 38px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
      color: black;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-weight: 800;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }

    .step-title {
      font-size: 17px;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .step-desc {
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .visual-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
    }

    .chunk-list,
    .retrieved-list {
      display: grid;
      gap: 14px;
      margin-top: 18px;
    }

    .chunk {
      padding: 18px;
      border-radius: 18px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
      transition: 0.3s ease;
      position: relative;
    }

    .chunk:hover {
      transform: translateY(-3px);
    }

    .chunk-id {
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--secondary);
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .chunk-text {
      line-height: 1.7;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #e5ecff;
    }

    .score {
      position: absolute;
      top: 18px;
      right: 18px;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: rgba(74,222,128,0.12);
      color: #86efac;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 700;
      border: 1px solid rgba(74,222,128,0.2);
    }

    .response-box {
      margin-top: 18px;
      padding: 24px;
      border-radius: 22px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(74,222,128,0.08), rgba(96,165,250,0.08));
      border: 1px solid rgba(96,165,250,0.15);
      line-height: 1.9;
      color: #eef4ff;
      min-height: 160px;
      white-space: pre-wrap;
    }

    .legend {
      display: flex;
      gap: 16px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      margin-top: 20px;
    }

    .legend-item {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    .legend-box {
      width: 18px;
      height: 18px;
      border-radius: 6px;
    }

    .green { background: rgba(74,222,128,0.4); }
    .blue { background: rgba(96,165,250,0.4); }
    .purple { background: rgba(139,92,246,0.4); }

    .explain {
      line-height: 1.9;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .tiny {
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: 10px;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    @media(max-width: 1300px) {
      .pipeline {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      }
    }

    @media(max-width: 1000px) {
      .layout,
      .visual-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }

    @media(max-width: 768px) {
      h1 {
        font-size: 42px;
      }

      .pipeline {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="container">

    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Interactive <span class="gradient">RAG Simulator</span></h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        Learn Retrieval-Augmented Generation visually. This simulator demonstrates how modern AI systems process documents,
        chunk data, create embeddings, retrieve relevant context, and generate grounded responses using vector similarity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="layout">

      <div class="sidebar">

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            Knowledge Base
          </div>

          <textarea id="knowledgeBase">RAG stands for Retrieval-Augmented Generation. It combines retrieval systems with large language models.

Vector databases store embeddings generated from document chunks.

Embeddings convert text into numerical vector representations.

Chunking breaks large documents into smaller semantic sections.

Retrieval systems search for the most relevant chunks using similarity search.

The LLM receives both the user query and retrieved context.

Grounded responses reduce hallucinations and improve factual accuracy.

RAG is commonly used in enterprise AI assistants, internal search, and support systems.

Popular vector databases include Pinecone, Weaviate, ChromaDB, and FAISS.</textarea>

          <div class="tiny">
            Modify the knowledge base to see how chunking and retrieval changes.
          </div>

          <div class="button-row">
            <button class="primary-btn" onclick="ingestDocuments()">Ingest Documents</button>
            <button class="secondary-btn" onclick="loadSample()">Load Example</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            User Query
          </div>

          <input id="queryInput" value="How does RAG reduce hallucinations?" />

          <div class="button-row">
            <button class="primary-btn" onclick="runRAG()">Run RAG Pipeline</button>
          </div>

          <div class="legend">
            <div class="legend-item">
              <div class="legend-box green"></div>
              Retrieved Context
            </div>

            <div class="legend-item">
              <div class="legend-box blue"></div>
              Embedding Space
            </div>

            <div class="legend-item">
              <div class="legend-box purple"></div>
              Generated Output
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="main">

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            RAG Pipeline
          </div>

          <div class="pipeline">

            <div class="step" id="step1">
              <div class="step-number">1</div>
              <div class="step-title">Ingestion</div>
              <div class="step-desc">
                Documents are uploaded into the system.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="step" id="step2">
              <div class="step-number">2</div>
              <div class="step-title">Chunking</div>
              <div class="step-desc">
                Large text is split into smaller semantic chunks.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="step" id="step3">
              <div class="step-number">3</div>
              <div class="step-title">Embeddings</div>
              <div class="step-desc">
                Text chunks are converted into vectors.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="step" id="step4">
              <div class="step-number">4</div>
              <div class="step-title">Retrieval</div>
              <div class="step-desc">
                Similarity search finds relevant chunks.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="step" id="step5">
              <div class="step-number">5</div>
              <div class="step-title">Generation</div>
              <div class="step-desc">
                LLM generates a grounded response using retrieved context.
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="visual-grid">

          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-title">
              <span class="dot"></span>
              Chunked Documents
            </div>

            <div class="chunk-list" id="chunkContainer"></div>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-title">
              <span class="dot"></span>
              Retrieved Context
            </div>

            <div class="retrieved-list" id="retrievedContainer"></div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            Generated Response
          </div>

          <div class="response-box" id="responseBox">
            Run the RAG pipeline to generate an answer.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            What Is Happening Internally?
          </div>

          <div class="explain" id="explanation">
            The simulator will explain each stage of the Retrieval-Augmented Generation process as you run it.
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </section>

  </div>

  <script>

    let chunks = [];

    function activateStep(stepId) {
      document.querySelectorAll('.step').forEach(step => {
        step.classList.remove('active');
      });

      document.getElementById(stepId).classList.add('active');
    }

    function ingestDocuments() {
      activateStep('step1');

      const text = document.getElementById('knowledgeBase').value;

      chunks = text
        .split(/\n+/)
        .map(chunk => chunk.trim())
        .filter(chunk => chunk.length > 0);

      setTimeout(() => {
        activateStep('step2');
        renderChunks();

        document.getElementById('explanation').innerHTML = `
          <strong>Document Ingestion:</strong><br><br>
          The system first receives raw documents. In production RAG systems this could include PDFs,
          websites, Notion pages, Jira tickets, databases, Slack messages, or enterprise documents.<br><br>

          <strong>Chunking:</strong><br><br>
          The documents are broken into smaller semantic chunks because LLMs cannot efficiently search entire documents.
          Chunking improves retrieval precision and keeps context windows manageable.
        `;
      }, 600);

      setTimeout(() => {
        activateStep('step3');
      }, 1200);
    }

    function renderChunks() {
      const container = document.getElementById('chunkContainer');
      container.innerHTML = '';

      chunks.forEach((chunk, index) => {
        const div = document.createElement('div');
        div.className = 'chunk';

        div.innerHTML = `
          <div class="chunk-id">CHUNK ${index + 1}</div>
          <div class="chunk-text">${chunk}</div>
        `;

        container.appendChild(div);
      });
    }

    function similarity(query, text) {
      const queryWords = query.toLowerCase().split(/\W+/);
      const textWords = text.toLowerCase().split(/\W+/);

      let matches = 0;

      queryWords.forEach(word => {
        if(textWords.includes(word)) {
          matches++;
        }
      });

      return matches / queryWords.length;
    }

    function runRAG() {

      if(chunks.length === 0) {
        ingestDocuments();
      }

      activateStep('step4');

      const query = document.getElementById('queryInput').value;

      const rankedChunks = chunks.map(chunk => ({
        text: chunk,
        score: similarity(query, chunk)
      }))
      .sort((a,b) => b.score - a.score)
      .slice(0,3);

      const retrievedContainer = document.getElementById('retrievedContainer');
      retrievedContainer.innerHTML = '';

      rankedChunks.forEach((item, index) => {
        const div = document.createElement('div');
        div.className = 'chunk';

        div.innerHTML = `
          <div class="chunk-id">RETRIEVED ${index + 1}</div>
          <div class="score">Similarity ${(item.score * 100).toFixed(0)}%</div>
          <div class="chunk-text">${item.text}</div>
        `;

        retrievedContainer.appendChild(div);
      });

      setTimeout(() => {
        activateStep('step5');

        const combinedContext = rankedChunks.map(r => r.text).join(' ');

        const response = `
User Query:
"${query}"

Retrieved Context:
${combinedContext}

LLM Response:
Based on the retrieved context, RAG reduces hallucinations because the language model is grounded using external retrieved knowledge instead of relying only on pre-trained memory.

The retrieval step fetches the most relevant chunks from the vector database and injects them into the prompt before generation.

This allows the AI system to produce more factual, contextual, and up-to-date answers.
        `;

        document.getElementById('responseBox').innerText = response;

        document.getElementById('explanation').innerHTML = `
          <strong>Embeddings:</strong><br><br>
          Each chunk was converted into a numerical vector representation called an embedding.
          Embeddings allow semantic similarity search instead of simple keyword matching.<br><br>

          <strong>Vector Retrieval:</strong><br><br>
          The query embedding was compared against stored chunk embeddings using similarity scoring.
          The top relevant chunks were retrieved from the vector database.<br><br>

          <strong>Augmented Generation:</strong><br><br>
          The retrieved chunks were injected into the LLM prompt.
          The LLM then generated a response grounded in external context instead of relying purely on training memory.
        `;

      }, 1200);
    }

    function loadSample() {
      document.getElementById('knowledgeBase').value = `RAG architectures are widely used in enterprise AI systems.

Retrieval-Augmented Generation improves factual grounding.

Embedding models convert text into high-dimensional vectors.

Chunk overlap helps preserve semantic continuity between text sections.

Vector databases allow fast similarity search at scale.

Prompt augmentation injects retrieved knowledge into the LLM context window.

Hybrid retrieval combines keyword search and vector search.

Re-ranking models improve retrieval relevance.

RAG pipelines are used in customer support bots, enterprise search, legal AI, and internal copilots.`;

      ingestDocuments();
    }

    ingestDocuments();

  </script>

</body>
</html>
